# vi(1)

## NAME

vi - a small vi-style text editor

## SYNOPSIS

    vi [+LINE | +] [FILE]

## DESCRIPTION

Edits a text file on the terminal, with the commonly used commands of POSIX vi. It starts in normal mode, where keys are commands. Press `i` to type text and `Esc` to go back to normal mode. Type `:wq` and press Enter to save and quit, or `:q!` to quit without saving. Standard input and output must be a terminal.

`+LINE` starts at that line, and `+` alone at the last line.

## MOTIONS

- `h j k l`, arrows: left, down, up, right
- `w b e`, `W B E`: words
- `0 ^ $`: start, first non-blank, end of the line
- `gg G`, `NG`: first, last, N-th line
- `f t F T` + char, `; ,`: find a character on the line
- `%`: matching bracket
- `H M L`: top, middle, bottom of the screen
- `Ctrl+F Ctrl+B`, `PgDn PgUp`: page down, up
- `Ctrl+D Ctrl+U Ctrl+E Ctrl+Y`: scroll

## EDITING

- `i a I A o O`: insert text (Esc ends)
- `x X`: delete a character
- `d c y` + motion, `dd cc yy`, `D C Y`: delete, change, yank
- `p P`: put after, before
- `r` + char, `s S`, `J`, `~`: replace, substitute, join lines, toggle case
- `u`, `Ctrl+R`: undo, redo
- `.`: repeat the last change
- `/ ?` + pattern, `n N`: search forward, backward (basic regular expressions)
- `ZZ`: save and quit

A count before a command repeats it, for example `3dd`.

## COMMANDS

- `:w [FILE]`, `:w! FILE`: write
- `:q`, `:q!`: quit
- `:wq`, `:x`: write and quit
- `:e!`: reload the file
- `:N`: go to line N
- `:[RANGE]s/PATTERN/REPLACEMENT/[g]`: substitute (RANGE is `N`, `N,M`, `.`, `$` or `%`)
- `:[RANGE]d`: delete lines
- `:set nu`, `:set nonu`, `:set ic`, `:set noic`: line numbers, ignore case

## NOTES

Ctrl+V and Shift+Insert paste in the client, and a paste in normal mode runs as commands. Press `i` first. There are no macros, visual mode, multiple files, or shell commands.

## SEE ALSO

nano(1), grep(1)
